/-!
# The final assertion of Stacks Tag 01NK

Let `A` be a graded ring, `X = Proj A`, `T` a scheme, `L` an invertible `𝒪_T`-module and
`ψ : A → Γ_*(T, L)` a graded map, in the degreewise spelling
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFullGraded.GradedSections`. [Stacks, Tag 01NK] attaches to `ψ`
the morphism `r_{L, ψ} : U(ψ) ⟶ X` (`…GradedSections.glued`) and the map of `ℤ`-graded algebras
`θ : r_{L, ψ}^*(⨁_d 𝒪_X(d)) ⟶ ⨁_d L^{⊗ d}|_{U(ψ)}`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartGradedThetaBuild.theta`), and ends with:

> Moreover, for any `d ≥ 1` and any open subscheme `V ⊂ T` such that the sections in `ψ(A_d)`
> generate `L^{⊗ d}|_V` the morphism `r_{L, ψ}|_V` agrees with the morphism `φ : V → Proj(A)` and
> the map `θ|_V` agrees with the map `α : φ^*𝒪_X(d) → L^{⊗ d}|_V` where `(φ, α)` is the pair of
> [Stacks, Tag 01N8] associated to `ψ|_{A^{(d)}} : A^{(d)} → Γ_*(V, L^{⊗ d})`.

This file proves that assertion, `moreover`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartGradedThetaMoreover.moreover` — **the final assertion of
  [Stacks, Tag 01NK]**, for every `d ≥ 1` and every open `V ⊆ T` on which `ψ(A_d)` generates
  `L^{⊗ d}`: the pair of [Stacks, Tag 01N8] for the Veronese restriction of `ψ|_V` exists and is
  unique, and for that pair `(φ, α)` one has `r_{L, ψ}|_V = φ` and `θ|_V = α` in degree `d`, as
  morphisms of sheaves of modules on `V`.
* `…psiSection_veroneseAt` — the trivialising section `ψ(g)` that [Stacks, Tag 01N8] attaches to
  the Veronese restriction of a graded map `φ` is `φ(g)` itself, through the left unitor; the
  coherence behind it is `…powVeroneseIso_one_hom_powCongr`.
* `…eq_hom_of_app_pullbackDegreeSection` — a morphism `φ^*𝒪_X(d) ⟶ M` that sends the pullback of
  the section of each `g ∈ A_d` to `ψ(g)` is the `α` of [Stacks, Tag 01N8].

## How the clause is read

* "`ψ(A_d)` generates `L^{⊗ d}|_V`" is `V ≤ ⨆_{g ∈ A_d} T_{ψ(g)}`: by [Stacks, Tag 01CY] a family
  of sections of an invertible module generates it at a point exactly when one of them does not
  vanish there. In particular `V ⊆ U(ψ)`, and `r_{L, ψ}|_V` is `r_{L, ψ}` precomposed with the
  inclusion `j : V ⟶ U(ψ)`.
* `ψ|_{A^{(d)}} : A^{(d)} → Γ_*(V, L^{⊗ d})` is the Veronese restriction
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartGradedVeronese.veroneseAt` of the inverse image
  `ψ|_V = GradedSections.pullback V.ι ψ`, whose values lie in the powers of `(L|_V)^{⊗ d}`.
* "the pair of [Stacks, Tag 01N8]" is a pair `p = (φ, α)` satisfying that tag's compatibility
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.IsCompatible`; the first conjunct of
  `moreover` says there is exactly one, and the second is stated for it.
* `θ|_V` in degree `d` is the inverse image along `j` of the degree-`d` component of `θ`, a map
  `j^* r_{L, ψ}^* 𝒪_X(d) ⟶ j^*(L^{⊗ d}|_{U(ψ)})`. To compare it with `α`, its source is identified
  with `φ^*𝒪_X(d)` through `r_{L, ψ} ∘ j = φ` (`Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr` and
  `Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp`), and its target with `(L|_V)^{⊗ d}` through the canonical
  comparisons: restriction to `U(ψ)` is inverse image along the open immersion
  (`Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback`), inverse image along `U(ψ) ⟶ T` after inverse
  image along `j` is inverse image along `V ⟶ T` (`Scheme.Modules.pullbackComp`,
  `Scheme.Modules.pullbackCongr`), the integer tensor power in nonnegative degree is the iterated
  one (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentMulSections.powCompare`), and inverse image commutes with
  tensor powers (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartRatioPullback.pullbackNatTensorPowIso`).

## The proof

As in the source: `(φ, α)` is pinned down by the sections `ψ(g)`, `g ∈ A_d`. For the morphism,
`φ` is the glued chart morphism (`…ProjChartGradedClassifying.classifyingHom_eq_glued`), and over
`V` the morphism `r_{L, ψ}` is that glued morphism
(`…ProjChartGradedVeroneseOpen.homOfLE_glued_eq_gluedVeronese_pullback`). For the map, both sides
are morphisms out of `φ^*𝒪_X(d)`, which `α` identifies with the invertible module `(L|_V)^{⊗ d}`
generated by the `ψ(g)`; so it suffices that both send the pullback of the section of `g` to
`ψ(g)|_V`. For `α` this is its normalisation; for `θ|_V` it is clause (2) of the tag
(`…ProjChartGradedTriple.isClauseTwo_theta`), followed through each comparison above by its
action on pulled-back global sections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CY)
-/

